IO-41: reject a malformed number in a math expression

getNumber() detected an exponent marker with no digits ("5e", "2.5E+") in a
local flag and returned 0 without setting the parser's error flag, and it
read a decimal point with no digits (".") as atof(".") = 0. The expression
was accepted with 0 in place of the constant. Set Err in both cases, so the
expression is rejected with ERROR 233 like any other syntax error.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-41_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
index c39dff7..910283b 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/mathexpr.c
@@ -243,8 +243,15 @@ double getNumber()
         }
     }
     Pos--;
-    if (errflag) return 0;
-    else return atof(sNumber);
+
+    /* --- a number with no digits (".") or no exponent digits ("5e")
+           is an error */
+    if (errflag || !(isDigit(sNumber[0]) || isDigit(sNumber[1])))
+    {
+        Err = 1;
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return atof(sNumber);
 }
 
